    <summary>Prometheus exporter for Windows machines.</summary>
    <description>
Prometheus exporter for Windows machines.

Installs the official MSI for the native architecture, AMD64 (x64) or ARM64, as the `windows_exporter` Windows service. 32-bit Windows is not supported. Metrics are served at `http://localhost:9182/metrics`. No firewall rule is created by default.

Full documentation: [package README](https://github.com/allxm4/windows-exporter#readme)

### Package parameters

- `/EnabledCollectors:` - Comma-separated collectors, as `--collectors.enabled`. `[defaults]` stands for the default collectors, for example `[defaults],process`.
- `/ConfigFile:` - YAML config file, as `--config.file`. Must exist before installing. Defaults to `config.yaml` in the install folder.
- `/ListenAddress:` - IP address to listen on. Defaults to all addresses.
- `/ListenPort:` - Port to listen on, 1 to 65535. Defaults to `9182`.
- `/MetricsPath:` - URL path of the metrics, as `--telemetry.path`. Must start with `/` and must not be `/health`. Defaults to `/metrics`.
- `/TextFileDirs:` - Comma-separated folders for the `textfile` collector, which is not enabled by default. Defaults to `textfile_inputs` in the install folder.
- `/TextFileDir:` - Older name of `/TextFileDirs:`.
- `/RemoteAddresses:` - Comma-separated remote addresses the firewall rule allows. Only used with `/AddLocal:FirewallException`.
- `/ExtraFlags:` - Other windows_exporter flags, separated by spaces, for example `--log.level=debug`. A flag's value can't contain spaces or quotes. Not for `--config.file` or `--collectors.enabled`.
- `/AddLocal:FirewallException` - Creates an inbound Windows Firewall rule for the exporter.
- `/Remove:FirewallException` - Disables that installer feature.

Example: `choco install prometheus-windows-exporter.install --params "'/EnabledCollectors:cpu,logical_disk,memory,os /ListenPort:9100 /AddLocal:FirewallException'"`

Paths may contain spaces; comma-separated lists must not. Package parameters take priority over the config file. All flags, collectors and installer properties are in the [windows_exporter README](https://github.com/prometheus-community/windows_exporter/blob/v0.32.1/README.md). Installer properties without a parameter, such as `APPLICATIONFOLDER`, can be passed with `--install-arguments`.

### Upgrading

Upgrades don't keep package parameters. Enable the `useRememberedArgumentsForUpgrades` feature, pass the same `--params` again, or keep your settings in the config file.

New minor versions can remove collectors and settings and rename metrics, and the service won't start while a removed one is in use. Upgrading from 0.30.x: read the [0.31.0 release notes](https://github.com/prometheus-community/windows_exporter/releases/tag/v0.31.0) and the [0.32 upgrade guide](https://github.com/prometheus-community/windows_exporter/blob/main/docs/upgrade/0.32.md).

### Security

Metrics are served over plain HTTP without authentication. Limit the firewall rule with `/RemoteAddresses:`, and use `--web.config.file` for TLS or basic authentication. Don't put secrets in package parameters; they appear in the Chocolatey and MSI logs.

### Issues

Package problems: leave a comment below or use Contact Maintainers, with your `choco` command and `chocolatey.log`. Exporter problems: [windows_exporter issues](https://github.com/prometheus-community/windows_exporter/issues).

</description>
